{"id": "unknown-2026-08-16-004", "date": "2026-08-16", "time_tags": {"year": 2026, "quarter": "Q3", "month": 8, "week": 33, "weekday": "Sun"}, "entities": {"companies": [], "customers": [], "suppliers": []}, "topics": ["supply_chain_shift", "earnings"], "sentiment": {"label": "positive", "score": 0.5, "keywords": ["growth"]}, "importance": {"score": 0.75, "reasons": ["涉及財報"]}, "title": "India Inc. starts FY27 on firmer footing than anticipated: ICRA", "content": "ICRA said the Indian corporate sector began FY27 on a firmer footing than anticipated, with aggregate revenues of its sample set of 838 listed firms growing by 22 per cent YoY in Q1. \nHowever, headline aggregate operating profit margin contracted by over 200 bps YoY in Q1 FY27 and net profits were flattish, mainly because of the oil-refining sector.  \nRevenue growth lagged in export-focused textile firms. ", "sources": [{"name": "fibre2fashion_textile", "url": "https://www.fibre2fashion.com/news/textile-news/india-inc-starts-fy27-on-firmer-footing-than-anticipated-icra-312691-newsdetails.htm", "type": "rss"}]}
